---
import { REPO_URL } from "../lib/releases"

const principles = [
  {
    title: "Pause and resume only where the protocol allows it",
    body: "The queue checks what the server supports before showing a control. If a transfer has to restart, it says so.",
  },
  {
    title: "Host keys are verified, never trusted silently",
    body: "SFTP connections fail closed on an unknown or changed fingerprint. You see the key before it is remembered.",
  },
  {
    title: "Credentials never leave the keychain",
    body: "Configuration files, diagnostics exports and logs contain connection details, never passwords or passphrases.",
  },
]
---

<section class="section" id="principles">
  <div class="container principles">
    <div>
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Honest by construction</p>
        <h2>No invented states</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          Most clients guess, then draw a progress bar and hope. sftply reports what the protocol
          actually did, including when the answer is "not supported".
        </p>
      </div>

      <blockquote class="pull-quote">
        A transfer queue is a promise. If the server cannot resume a download, the interface should
        not offer a resume button.
        <span>Design principle · <a href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`}>architecture notes</a></span>
      </blockquote>
    </div>

    <ol class="principle-list">
      {
        principles.map((principle) => (
          <li class="principle">
            <div>
              <h3>{principle.title}</h3>
              <p>{principle.body}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>
